                "evidence": "review changes_requested: duetflow/app.py:20-24 and 167-169 still map `duetflow collect` to `cmd_not_yet`. Concrete input: `python3 -m duetflow.app collect` prints that Collection arrives in phase 02 and exits 2, so the operator cannot run the manual Collections required by docs/PLAN.md \u00a72 and lines 326-329 while the timer is deferred; the new collector is unreachable through the shipped CLI and stores no plays.; duetflow/collector.py:18-40 never checks elapsed time against `collection.max_collection_gap_minutes`. With the newest stored Play more than 90 minutes old, Collection stores whatever remains in Spotify's 50-item window and returns normally without warning, contrary to docs/ROADMAP.md:125-130; the operator is not told that older Plays may already have been lost silently and irrecoverably.; duetflow/collector.py:32 normalizes Spotify's `played_at` through `to_iso`, which drops fractional seconds before the value reaches the natural key. Concrete input: two items for track `same` at `2026-01-01T10:00:00.100Z` and `2026-01-01T10:00:00.900Z` make `collect` report one new Play and store one row at `2026-01-01T10:00:00+00:00`; two distinct Plays are collapsed, corrupting the evidence used for Current Rotation and violating I8's natural-key semantics.; duetflow/spotify.py:148-166 handles a 401 from `GET /me/player/recently-played` by immediately raising `SpotifyError`; the function accepts no refresh credentials or callback, so an expired access token cannot be refreshed once and retried as docs/PLAN.md:249-256 requires. A Collection with an expired access token therefore aborts and may permanently miss Plays as the 50-item window advances.; duetflow/spotify.py:148-166 handles a 429 by immediately raising a generic `SpotifyError`; it neither honors `Retry-After` nor inspects `reason: QUOTA_EXCEEDED` as docs/PLAN.md:249-256 requires. An ordinary rate limit followed by an available successful response is attempted only once, aborting the Collection and risking perma",
