                "evidence": "review changes_requested: duetflow/collector.py:34-41 derives collection.max_collection_gap_minutes from the newest stored Play instead of the previous successful Collection, and tests/test_collector.py:test_a_stale_newest_play_warns_that_plays_may_be_lost enshrines that mismatch. Concrete input: run two successful Collections one minute apart when the newest Play is a day old; the second Collection emits a warning that Plays may have been lost even though polling was on time. With successful empty Collections there is no last-Collection state at all. This contradicts docs/PLAN.md \u00a76, makes the data-loss warning untrustworthy, and must track successful Collection time rather than playback time.; duetflow/app.py:150-160 closes refresh() over the original account and therefore always submits account.refresh_token even after Spotify rotates it. Concrete input: a stale access token is proactively refreshed from R1 to R2, then the new access token receives 401; the required refresh-and-retry submits invalidated R1 again, exits with InvalidGrant/re-consent guidance, and stores no Plays. The retry must use the latest rotated refresh token so a transient 401 does not create a false credential-expiry failure and risk Play loss.",
